# The hull of two intervals with 2-limb bounds (milestone2.md, "One enclosure interface"): the
# listing of interval_hull_1 on the comparison of two limbs, lt_2_2, each bound selected limb by
# limb. Exact; the hull with the empty set ((+inf, 0), (-inf, 0)) is the other operand. For every
# precision.
kernel:        interval_hull_2
input:         xl = xl0 xl1
input:         xu = xu0 xu1
input:         yl = yl0 yl1
input:         yu = yu0 yu1
output:        zl = zl0 zl1
output:        zu = zu0 zu1
requires:      interval xl xu
requires:      interval yl yu
ensures:       interval_set zl zu union x=xl,xu y=yl,yu
min_precision: 1
source:        the smaller lower bound and the larger upper bound, by lt_2_2 (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeIntervalExact.v interval_hull_2_correct
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the bounds are selected among the bounds of the operands; interval_set states what comes out for every pair of canonical intervals

ml  = lt_2_2(yl0, yl1, xl0, xl1)
zl0 = select(ml, yl0, xl0)
zl1 = select(ml, yl1, xl1)
mu  = lt_2_2(xu0, xu1, yu0, yu1)
zu0 = select(mu, yu0, xu0)
zu1 = select(mu, yu1, xu1)
